{
  "abstract": "For every integer r ≥ 3 there is a δ > 0 such that every real number in [1 − δ, 1] is the ordinary Turán density of a family of finite simple r-uniform hypergraphs. The family may be infinite. Its density is the limit of the largest number of edges in an n-vertex hypergraph avoiding the family, divided by the binomial coefficient n choose r. This formalizes Theorem 1.1 of Liu and Pikhurko.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Xizhi Liu"
    }
  ],
